This was a desk run, so I printed the git commands and ran none of them. That means no `FILED` lines, and nothing was committed or pushed.

- **Check results:** `3c09-registry-agent` and `3c10-registry-task` passed all three checks, so their filing commands are listed above. `3c11-home-path` failed the profile check at line 11 because it contains a home path. It needs that path removed or changed to a generic `~/` path before it can be filed.
- **Registry values weren't checked:** this session has no bus, so the profile check had no agent or task registry to compare against. It only used values from this machine (its hostname, credential key names and home paths). The two registry notes passed on that basis. If they contain agent ids or task ids from a real mesh, this check would not have caught them.
- **A real run would fail:** `repos/solo-space` isn't a git repository (`git -C … rev-parse` says "not a git repository"). So it has no `origin` to fetch from or push to, and the first `fetch` would fail. Before a real filing, it needs to be a clone of the space's remote.
- **Commands left out:** I didn't list the ones that only run in some cases: the skip-path `log -1 … origin/main`, `reset -q HEAD~1` after a failed re-check, and `rebase --abort` after a conflict. The re-check after the rebase runs `check.sh`, not git, so it isn't in the list either.

